# `wl_keyboard.keymap` serves these bytes verbatim, and the keymap gate checks
# their length — an EOL conversion would change every byte count (.notes/wayland.md §6.12).
crates/servers/data/*.xkb binary

# Shell scripts are checked out LF whatever `core.autocrlf` is set to, so they
# run from a Linux guest (WSL) against a Windows checkout as well as on CI. A
# CRLF smudge makes `sh tools/...` fail with `$'\r': command not found`.
*.sh text eol=lf
